course: dictionary
lesson: 14170
title: Modified: changed a little
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: When something is modified, it has been changed, usually a little, to make it better or to suit a new purpose. «The bike had a modified seat that was taller and softer.» The seat was not made from scratch. Someone changed it so it fitted a rider better.
explain: Modified often sits next to a helpful word, like slightly or genetically. «The recipe was slightly modified, with less sugar.» Slightly tells you the change was small. Genetically modified means scientists changed the genes of a living thing.
explain: In grammar, a word is modified when another word describes or limits it. In «a tiny ant», the word tiny modifies ant, because it tells you what kind of ant. Check the clues around the word, and ask what has been changed or described.
fact: Modified means changed, usually a little, to make something better or to suit a new purpose.
fact: «Genetically modified» means that scientists have changed the genes of a plant or animal.
fact: Genetically modified crops are a topic people debate, so people have different opinions about them.
fact: In grammar, a word is modified when another word describes or limits it.
exercise: «The bike had a modified seat that was taller and softer.» What does modified mean here? | Broken and thrown away | Brand new and never used | *Changed a little to suit a new purpose | Painted a bright colour
exercise: «Scientists have genetically modified this crop so it grows in dry soil.» What does genetically modified mean? | Cut and dried in the sun | *Having its genes changed by scientists | Sold in a shop | Grown on a farm by a family
exercise: In «a tiny ant», the word tiny modifies another word. Which word is modified? | a | tiny | *ant
test: «The recipe was slightly modified, with less sugar.» What does slightly modified mean? | Made completely new | *Changed a little | Thrown away | Copied word for word
test: «Our teacher modified the rule so that everyone could join in.» What does modified show? | The rule was never used | The rule was read aloud | *The rule was changed | The rule was lost
exam: «The first version of the game was tricky, so the team made a modified version for younger players.» What does a modified version mean? | *A version changed a little to suit a different group | A version made only for adults | A version that is broken | A version copied exactly from the first
